# rm571, the soap-map swimmer (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm571
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent none
tier standard
written_for rmx_moll_coldharbour
written_by codex
title the soap-map swimmer
fits stage=young|adolescent|adult|old
prefers talk=quiet honesty=guarded
traits temper=even talk=quiet warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=guarded piety=ordinary drive=steady
quirk draws_soap_maps_on_a_tile_with_the_wet_street_apart
likes hard_cheese swimming tidy_house first_warm_day
dislikes bad_manners cold_tea
fears a_dry_change_of_clothes_falling_in_a_puddle a_whisper_that_leaves_the_wrong_name_behind
hopes a_dry_shelf_above_a_place_fit_for_swimming
topics weather +0.6 travel +0.4 home +0.4 smalltalk +0.3
styles comfort=quiet gossip=closed refuse=quiet tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# marks low streets in soap on a tile and keeps the highest corner clear for imagining where dry clothes ought to wait after a swim.

words
oath! = A drip on my dry corner | Wash out the hill
saying! = Save a corner for the towel | The first puddle draws itself
tile = my pale scrap of tile | a piece of clean tile
soap = a thin yellow soap chip | a soft soap end
slope = the sloping soap line | my crooked little hill
bare = my clear corner of tile | the part left clean
towel = a thick folded towel | a dry piece of towel
cheese = a neat hard-cheese square | the cheese in my wrapper
tearing = a grey mark from cold tea | a flat cold ring
mild = the first soft air | the first warmth after winter
wipe = a dry bit of cloth | a little wiping rag
doorstep = a pale patch of doorstep | a sheltered step end
puddle = the first thin puddle | a low shine of street water

any
opinion @1 city for 1 : There are so many turns that one of them usually takes me to a street with dry feet.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : I like being told where a wet crossing starts without having to tell a whole private story in return.
opinion @1 houses mixed 0 : Tall doors have deep sills. A sill deep enough to keep the rain off suits me.
opinion @1 road mixed 0 : A road ought to keep one little dry edge until the people on it have finished getting home.
opinion @1 strangers mixed 0 : A stranger can ask for the way without asking where I sleep.
opinion @1 festivals mixed 0 : Once the final visitor goes, my street looks wide again and I can hear the gutter running.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : It makes sense to put a hot bowl within reach of a wolf just in from the cold.
line @1 greet : There's a dry bit to stand on, here.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : I haven't seen those feet on my map.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. I haven't wiped yesterday's hill off yet.
line @4 greet [here.time=dusk|night] : This evening drip hasn't reached my corner yet.
line @1 greet.return : Your greeting carried past that trickle nicely.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : I knew your voice before I looked up.
line @3 greet.return [self.working=yes] : I've a thumb free to hold my place.
line @4 greet.return [here.time=dusk|night] : Quiet carries nicely after the light goes.
line @1 kin.open [pair.kin!=no] : Kin may sit by the clean corner.
line @1 again.open : I left the soap where our road turned.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Friend, you can see the secret dry square.
line @1 farewell : Follow the paler strip along the road.
line @1 farewell.return : And tuck the towel up high.
line @1 react.news : Tell the part that hasn't washed away.
line @1 react.news.new : Fresh marks to me.
line @1 react.news.known : I know where that telling started.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I don't see the bit that joins up yet.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|loss|theft|assault|arrest|crime] : We can leave the little lines alone a while.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|succession|work] : Such a day deserves the clean corner.
line @1 ask.how : How wet did you get out there?
line @1 answer.how : Nearly dry, apart from one patch.
line @1 thank : I'll remember whose hand kept my towel dry.
line @1 deflect_thanks : It didn't take much soap to show the way.
line @1 sympathise : I'll shift my bundle and sit where your voice carries.
line @1 reassure : One bit of street dries before the rest.
line @1 decline : That bit of the business can stay under my towel.
line @1 accept_decline : All right. I'll wipe the extra mark off.
line @1 preclose : I can feel the evening coming up the hill.
line @1 accept_preclose : We'll leave the tile clean for tomorrow.
scene water_word
when topic=news world.news
does tell.news / react.self / assess
a : The words came through #world.news_from#. #world.news#. | #world.news#. The place tagged on the account was #world.news_from#.
b : Can you show me on the tile? | Have you anything to add?
a : I can repeat the words that reached my own ears. The little map is just the streets I know. | I'd leave that bit of the tile clear till there's more to hear.

scene private_soap
when topic=gossip here.gossip=yes
does tell.gossip / react.self / assess
a : Some talk leaves more of a mark than a whole piece of soap. | A whisper came my way with another wolf's name fixed to it.
b : Are you rubbing it off? | Will you draw it?
a : I'm leaving it off my own tile. | Wet streets belong here. Somebody's private name can stay out of the puddle.

story map_spoon [topic=memories|weather]
  : I poured a spoonful onto my tile to see which street was lowest.
  : Three roads went wet before I noticed my thumb was propping one side up.
  b : Did the hill disappear?
  : Only my extra hill. The real streets did much better once I put my thumb away.

story cheese_house [topic=food|memories]
  : I put a cheese square on the clean corner and built a row of soap houses round it.
  : After a while I forgot which bit had been my lunch and which was a rather tall roof.
  b : Did a nibble settle it?
  : A sniff. I have never needed quite so much education as a whole bite of house.

story folding_rain [topic=home|memories]
  : A towel lay folded neatly while a corner of the shelf took a leak from above.
  : When I opened the towel it had four wet marks all about the same size.
  b : Four leaks?
  : Just one with the advantage of a tidy fold. I moved the shelf before tidying again.

rule @dry_side
when concept=bark here.time=dawn
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Keep the clean corner turned uphill.

rule @fold_towel
when concept=bark here.time=dusk
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dry side facing the last bit of warmth.

rule @draw_rill
when concept=bark here.weather=rain
does aside
cooldown 8h
say There's a good little street appearing in the soap.

rule @bare_mark
when concept=bark here.place=street
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One pale slab still showing above the shine.

dlg @1 resident.hub : Stand beside my tile and leave the dry part clear, please.
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, you remember which corner I'd like to save.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : The tile can rest face down for a quiet word.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=hostile|wary] : State your business with the map resting where it is.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=child self.workplace] : I'm at lessons at #self.workplace#. My tile is for a different kind of drawing.
dlg @2 resident.job : I notice the turns where a little care can keep a good bundle dry.
dlg @1 resident.news [world.news] : It came by way of #world.news_from#. #world.news#.
dlg @1 resident.gossip [here.gossip=yes] : That talk wants a private mark. I keep those off this tile.
dlg @1 resident.bye : Mind where the road rises at the bend.
graft resident.hub
choice Why leave a clean corner on a map? -> tile_corner
node tile_corner
say When I draw a swimming place I mark the shelf where my things will stay dry. If the soap line crosses the clear part, I've put my towel too close to the water.
choice What if there's real rain? -> tile_rain
choice I'll leave the clear corner alone. -> hub
node tile_rain
say Then a little roof would be more use than a drawing. I'd tuck the things up high and keep the map for seeing which way to come home.
choice I'd like to see that homeward road. -> hub
choice I'll take the high way. -> bye


grown
scene old_wash
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Rubbing a thumb along a wet pane sometimes brings back my first little city of soap. | I still leave a corner of the map quite blank.
b : Did it work? | For a towel?
a : Well enough to teach me which questions needed a real walk in the rain. | Yes. I enjoy keeping the joke where only an old friend will see it.

scene dry_clothes
when topic=home
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When somebody comes in from a swim I offer a clean high shelf before any questions. | A quiet welcome begins with somewhere dry to put what's in your arms.
b : You swim too? | And conversation?
a : I learnt what a wet doorstep does to an unprotected bundle at a very early age. | When both hands are free enough for a cup.

scene patient_walk
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At a flooded turn I stand and read the ripples before choosing my route. | I like a map I can rub out as the road changes.
b : Does waiting help? | Even after a lot of work?
a : It lets the cart splash go first. There's often a perfectly dry path once it has passed. | A day's pride is no reason to send a visitor into deep water.

scene warm_wall
when topic=season here.season=spring
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Spring brings one moment when a stone wall stops feeling colder than the hand. | I test a folded towel for the first warmth a patch of stone can give.
b : Can you tell when? | For the old swimming ritual?
a : In one narrow corner, yes. I'd leave other wolves to speak for spring in their own streets. | For anybody coming in with cold shoulders.

scene quiet_place
when topic=dreams
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd like a place where the water's close and the changing shelf is dry. | Give me a shelf the highest winter water can't reach and I'd be comfortable.
b : How close? | Nothing on the shelf?
a : Within a friendly walk. I'd like the walk to remain part of it. | Towel, cheese, room for a second parcel. The contents could be very modest.


young
scene soap_city
when topic=pastimes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I draw the hill on #tile# with #soap#. | #bare.capitalize# is where I put the dry clothes.
b : Where's the river? | Are they tiny clothes?
a : The river does itself if I tip a spoon of water at the top. | They're pretend. Very easy to fold.

scene school_map
when topic=work self.job=child self.workplace
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : At #self.workplace# I can make a line straighter than my soap streets. | I've learnt how to write the name of a street without drawing its puddles.
b : Why don't you straighten the streets too? | Is that easier?
a : Because I'd lose my way the moment I followed those marks. | Quicker. It won't keep your foot out of the water.

scene swim_edge
when topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #towel.capitalize# goes higher than my head when I go swimming. | My favourite moment in a swim is when the water takes my whole weight.
b : How do you reach it again? | Is it cold?
a : I mean higher than my head is in the water. I'm taller on the step. | A bit. That's when I feel it carry my full weight.

scene hard_square
when topic=food self.likes=hard_cheese
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #cheese.capitalize# has the dry patch of my map. | I can nibble two streets in a piece of cheese.
b : Is it a house? | And the third?
a : Dinner. It is not a public building. | By the third turn there's hardly any city left.

scene first_warm
when topic=weather self.likes=first_warm_day
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #mild.capitalize# is when I stop walking round the sunny patch and go straight into it. | A sun-warmed stone has a smell I can catch standing up.
b : What does that feel like? | What smell comes off the stone?
a : Like somebody put the towel out specially. | My stone. Only less wet.

scene cold_cup
when topic=food self.dislikes=cold_tea
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : #tearing.capitalize# is a shore nobody wants to swim in. | I'd like the tea before it gets all flat.
b : What about a spoon? | Can it stand up?
a : The spoon is allowed. It doesn't have to drink anything. | No, but hot tea makes a little cloud. Cold tea just sits.

scene tidy_tile
when topic=home self.likes=tidy_house
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : With #wipe# I can tidy a whole town before anybody knocks. | I keep my clean towel separate from the one that wipes the tile.
b : Whose town? | Can you tell the two apart?
a : The soap one. A real town takes a much bigger rag. | Only after one of them's got a hill all over it.


adolescent
scene road_secret
when topic=travel
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I know which street will gutter first before the first proper shower. | I used to tip the whole hill towards my favourite corner.
b : Will you tell me how? | Have you changed the game?
a : Look where the dry silt lies. I'd like to keep one little way home for myself. | I draw the water along the way the street really sends it.

scene swim_plan
when topic=pastimes self.likes=swimming
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : For a swim I practise putting the clothes somewhere that will stay dry through an idle shower. | My favourite finish to a swim is a stone that's kept the sun.
b : Why practise? | Could you stay in all day?
a : Having to walk back in a wet shirt argued the case quite effectively. | Not if I'd promised myself a proper supper.

scene bad_manner
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=bad_manners
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wolf borrowing a tile could wait to be handed it the right way up. | I mind a caller who shifts somebody's drying coat so a bag can sit there.
b : Does it really matter? | Would you say anything?
a : A polite borrower gets a tile I've tipped dry. Unless you wanted it down your sleeve. | I'd offer the bag a different place. The coat has already waited its turn.

scene commons_map
when topic=home self.quarter=commons
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : My Commons map is gradually losing the lines nobody needs. | I keep the bit by one Commons turn unusually clean.
b : What did you leave off? | Do you live there?
a : Doors I'd drawn just because I knew who lived behind them. A street is enough. | It shows a high stone. Draw enough ink there and its useful height disappears.

scene soap_choice
when topic=smalltalk
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I used to call a blank space on a tile a secret. | #slope.capitalize# shows why the first drop chooses its direction.
b : What is it now? | Do you tell people the rest?
a : Somewhere I haven't had a good enough look at to draw an honest line. | If they need the crossing. I don't need to account for every journey I make.

scene no_name
when topic=lore here.region=ridgemere
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I care about how much water's on the street more than whose fine door it reached. | My own note can stay folded when somebody comes fishing for names.
b : Haven't you heard the names? | You keep a list?
a : Most streets have plenty. Just the height of the sill is relevant to my drawing. | I keep a small map of wet stone. No interviews come with it.
